   Thirty batches immediately before a fixed-window reset and thirty afterward allow 3,000 lines within a rolling 
minute. **Smallest fix:** describe 1,500 lines per fixed 60-second bucket and the boundary burst.

Folding the stream into the closed event `type` is compatible with BR-013. SPEC does not prescribe literal reason 
names, but T19 should document mappings for valid-session 401 responses and lease expiry.

The tests qualify as integration tests: Auth, application-user lookup, RPCs, and counters remain real; only Nextâ€™s 
cookie transport is substituted. Injection probes rejected newline enums and nonfinite numbers, ignored 
prototype/`toJSON` fields, and normalized `-0`. Received-byte limits and invalid UTF-8 handling behaved as claimed; 
cancellation returned promptly through Nextâ€™s installed request adapter.

Typecheck, touched-file lint, and tracked diff checks passed. Local read-only catalog queries confirmed the boolean 
limiter and its restricted grants. I did not rerun the DB/E2E suites or build under the read-only constraint. No 
online database was accessed.
