spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-1-# SPEC: Phase 5 — Messaging Resilience
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-2-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-3-Goal: In the production messaging drawer, no message a user 
sends is lost or duplicated across network and Realtime outages, reloads, several tabs, account changes, and several 
devices; typing, unread/read state, and @mention notifications stay live and correct; and messaging health is 
observable through redacted logs — without regressing existing messaging.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-4-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:5:Status: Final v4 — revised after adversarial reviews r2–r4 
(`reviews/sol-review-spec-r2.md` … `r4.md`); r4 fixes applied without a fifth review by owner decision D7 
(2026-10-06). Approved by the owner 2026-10-06 (native question UI: "Aprovada"). Interview rounds 1–2, confirmation, 
and owner decisions D1–D6 recorded in `state.md` (Verdict: Ready).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-6-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-7-## 1. Summary
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-8-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:9:The Virtual Office messaging drawer (`MessagingDrawer` → 
`MessageFeed` → `MessageComposer` / `MessageItem`, state in `MessagingContext`, data in `useMessages` / 
`useConversations`, Realtime in `useMessageSubscription` / `useConversationRealtime`, typing in 
`useConversationPresence`) was completed for timeline features in Phase 4. Phase 4 also delivered a failed send that 
keeps text/reply/files with a single-message retry (`clientMessageId` idempotency in `POST /api/messages/create`, 
stored in `messages.client_message_id`), a Realtime catch-up after reconnect, and opt-in desktop notifications for 
DM/group messages. This phase adds: a durable per-user outbox for text messages with server-fenced attempt generations 
and safe cross-tab and cross-account behavior; a connection banner; application-level recovery and health for every 
messaging Realtime stream with polling fallback; a reliable, named, members-only typing indicator; live cross-device 
unread/read sync; @mentions with desktop notifications (including rooms); messaging health metrics as redacted server 
logs; and two Phase 4 database follow-ups plus restoring the open conversation after reload.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-10-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-11-## 2. Problem statement
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-12-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-13-Workspace members using the chat on unstable networks or 
sleeping laptops lose work and trust: a send that fails must be retried by hand, a reload or closed tab discards it 
(the idempotency key lives only in component memory), and nothing tells the user the chat is disconnected. Optimistic 
messages are matched to stored ones by guessing from content and time. Realtime recovery is incomplete: the SDK 
retries errored/timed-out channels and the conversation-list stream invalidates the list after its own rejoins, but 
the application exposes health only for the messages channel, does not recover terminal closures of the 
conversation-list channel, has no aggregate health, and has no polling fallback, so new messages and unread counts can 
silently stop updating. The typing indicator disappears after ~4 s of continuous typing and is broadcast on a public 
channel. Reading on one device leaves stale unread badges on the user's other devices. Nobody can mention someone, so 
room conversations (which never notify) cannot reach a specific person. Nobody can tell in production whether 
messaging is healthy.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-14-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:15:## 3. Goals and success metrics
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-16-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-17-### Goals
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-18-- G1: A text message the user sends is never silently lost: it 
is delivered, pending, or visibly failed with an action.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-19-- G2: No message is ever stored or shown twice because of 
automatic resends, several tabs, lost or late responses, or account changes; a message is never stored under a 
different sender.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-20-- G3: Messaging recovers from network and Realtime outages 
without user action and keeps updating through polling while Realtime is down.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-21-- G4: Typing indicators are reliable, named, and visible only 
to conversation members.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-22-- G5: Unread/read state and own sent messages stay in sync 
across the same user's tabs and devices (≤ 5 s while connectivity is healthy).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-23-- G6: A user can @mention conversation members, and the 
mentioned person is notified on the desktop, including in rooms.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-24-- G7: Messaging health (latency, delivery, connection) is 
observable in technical logs without exposing content.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-25-- G8: No existing messaging behavior regresses; every database 
change reaches the online target in a controlled, verified way at phase end.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-26-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:27:### Success metrics
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-28-- With ≤ 10 pending messages and create quota available, all 
pending messages are delivered within 10 s after connectivity returns, without any click, in their original order, 
each exactly once; with more, delivery continues automatically within the server rate limit (D1).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-29-- With Realtime down and HTTP working, other members' new 
messages appear within 45 s of the outage start, and within 15 s (plus request time) of being sent once polling is 
active.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-30-- With healthy connectivity and Realtime, cross-device/tab sync 
of unread counts, read state, and own sent messages within 5 s (D4); during a Realtime outage the polling deadlines 
above apply.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-31-- Each flow is covered by a passing Playwright E2E test (two 
accounts, and two tabs / two devices where relevant) that passed 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-32-- The existing messaging regression E2E suite passes after each 
slice.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-33-- Every migration of the phase is applied to the online target 
`vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` at phase end with explicit owner authorization, catalog readback, and a runtime smoke check.
--
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-37-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-38-### Primary users
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-39-- All workspace members who use the chat in direct, group, and 
room conversations (members of `conversation_members`), as sender, recipient, or mentioned user.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-40-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-41-### Secondary users
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-42-- The same user on several tabs of one browser and on several 
devices/browsers at once; several users sharing one browser.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:43:- The owner/operator, who reads the messaging metric logs.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-44-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-45-### Stakeholders
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-46-- Owner (Giuliano): approves the SPEC, performs the final test, 
authorizes the online migrations at phase end, and deploys the application.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-47-
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-48-## 5. Scope
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md-49-
