spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:101:| FR-009 | An item not stored 24 h after the user pressed send 
is never sent automatically: once fenced as not stored, it shows as failed "expirada" with "Tentar de novo" and 
"Apagar"; an unknown item found stored resolves as delivered, never as expired. "Tentar de novo" on an expired item 
keeps the key and the original send time (for metrics) and starts a new 24 h delivery window, within which the normal 
transient/unknown rules apply. | Must | AC-010, AC-042 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:104:| FR-012 | Session end without explicit sign-out: an item is 
held (not failed, not deleted) only when the client's auth state reports the session ended (signed out, or refresh 
rejected); a 401 while the client still holds a valid session is treated as transient. Held items drain after the same 
user signs in again (subject to FR-009); another user on the browser never sees, sends, or deletes them. | Must | 
AC-012 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:119:| FR-027 | The client records metric events — send latency 
(press → server confirmed), outbox wait time, send outcomes by reason, Realtime stream drops/recoveries and outage 
duration, polling activations and duration — in a bounded buffer (oldest dropped when full) and sends them 
fire-and-forget in batches of at most 50 events and 16 KB, at most one delivery in flight, each aborted after 5 s, 
dropping batches under overload. The authenticated, per-user rate-limited route rejects oversized requests, accepts 
only closed event/reason enums and bounded numeric fields, drops anything else, adds a server-derived app version, and 
writes structured log lines under BR-013. | Must | AC-028 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:144:| BR-013 | Metric log lines contain only closed-enum event 
type and outcome/reason, bounded durations/counts, conversation type, timestamp, and server-derived app version — 
never message text, attachment names, conversation names, user names or emails, user/conversation identifiers, or any 
client-supplied free text. | R1-q12 B, R2-q2, confirmation point 9; review r2 #14 |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:160:- Structured metric log lines (BR-013).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:175:- No message text, names, or identifiers in metrics (BR-013); 
no external analytics service.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:220:| Malicious, oversized, hanging, or sustained metrics traffic 
| Rejected or dropped; route rate-limited; messaging unaffected (AC-028, AC-029). |
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:230:- Metrics: closed enums, bounded numbers and sizes, 
server-derived version, per-user rate limit, no free text (BR-013); unauthenticated requests are rejected and produce 
no metric log line.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:253:- AC-010 (FR-009, BR-006): Given a never-dispatched item whose 
send time is more than 24 h ago, when connectivity returns, then no create request is sent for it and it shows 
"expirada" with "Tentar de novo" / "Apagar"; "Tentar de novo" delivers it once; given a manual retry of an expired 
item that gets 429 and then an unknown outcome, it is retried/fenced automatically and stored once.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:271:- AC-028 (FR-027, BR-013): Given a send, a stream recovery, 
and a polling episode occur, then the metrics route writes structured lines with enum event type/reason, durations, 
and server-derived version; a scan finds no message text, names, emails, or user/conversation IDs; a payload with 
unknown fields, free-text strings, out-of-range numbers, or a forged version produces no such values in the logs; a 
request over 50 events or 16 KB is rejected; requests beyond the per-user rate limit are rejected; an unauthenticated 
request is rejected and produces no metric log line.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:278:- AC-035 (§12): The Supabase/RLS review gate passes for every 
migration, RLS/Realtime policy, repository, and API route change.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:285:- AC-042 (FR-006, FR-009): Given an unknown item whose request 
was actually stored, when A tries to cancel it or its 24 h passes, then no cancel is offered before fencing, the fence 
resolves it as delivered, and it never shows "expirada".
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:298:  - Integration (local Supabase Postgres/Realtime and real API 
routes): sender and attempt-generation fencing incl. stale requests and stale fences (AC-044, AC-045), insertion 
quota, request budget, and fence budget (AC-009), fence/lookup authorization incl. anon and other users' keys (AC-038, 
AC-042, AC-044), outcome classes (AC-046), mention atomicity/validation/replay/RLS (AC-024, AC-046), private 
typing-topic authorization incl. anon/outsider/public topic (AC-019), `mark_conversation_read` membership (AC-030), 
`get_unread_counts` anon revoke (AC-031), metrics route auth, enums, sizes, rate limit, redaction (AC-028).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:310:- Supabase/RLS review gate passed (AC-035).
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/SPEC.md:318:- Non-blocking: per-company or per-conversation metric 
breakdowns would need identifiers in logs, which BR-013 forbids; a later owner decision is required to add them.

