   1: # SPEC: Phase 5 — Messaging Resilience
   2: 
   3: Goal: In the production messaging drawer, no message a user sends is lost or duplicated across network and 
Realtime outages, reloads, several tabs, account changes, and several devices; typing, unread/read state, and @mention 
notifications stay live and correct; and messaging health is observable through redacted logs — without regressing 
existing messaging.
   4: 
   5: Status: Final v4 — revised after adversarial reviews r2–r4 (`reviews/sol-review-spec-r2.md` … `r4.md`); r4 fixes 
applied without a fifth review by owner decision D7 (2026-10-06). Approved by the owner 2026-10-06 (native question 
UI: "Aprovada"). Interview rounds 1–2, confirmation, and owner decisions D1–D6 recorded in `state.md` (Verdict: Ready).
   6: 
   7: ## 1. Summary
   8: 
   9: The Virtual Office messaging drawer (`MessagingDrawer` → `MessageFeed` → `MessageComposer` / `MessageItem`, 
state in `MessagingContext`, data in `useMessages` / `useConversations`, Realtime in `useMessageSubscription` / 
`useConversationRealtime`, typing in `useConversationPresence`) was completed for timeline features in Phase 4. Phase 
4 also delivered a failed send that keeps text/reply/files with a single-message retry (`clientMessageId` idempotency 
in `POST /api/messages/create`, stored in `messages.client_message_id`), a Realtime catch-up after reconnect, and 
opt-in desktop notifications for DM/group messages. This phase adds: a durable per-user outbox for text messages with 
server-fenced attempt generations and safe cross-tab and cross-account behavior; a connection banner; 
application-level recovery and health for every messaging Realtime stream with polling fallback; a reliable, named, 
members-only typing indicator; live cross-device unread/read sync; @mentions with desktop notifications (including 
rooms); messaging health metrics as redacted server logs; and two Phase 4 database follow-ups plus restoring the open 
conversation after reload.
  10: 
  11: ## 2. Problem statement
  12: 
  13: Workspace members using the chat on unstable networks or sleeping laptops lose work and trust: a send that fails 
must be retried by hand, a reload or closed tab discards it (the idempotency key lives only in component memory), and 
nothing tells the user the chat is disconnected. Optimistic messages are matched to stored ones by guessing from 
content and time. Realtime recovery is incomplete: the SDK retries errored/timed-out channels and the 
conversation-list stream invalidates the list after its own rejoins, but the application exposes health only for the 
messages channel, does not recover terminal closures of the conversation-list channel, has no aggregate health, and 
has no polling fallback, so new messages and unread counts can silently stop updating. The typing indicator disappears 
after ~4 s of continuous typing and is broadcast on a public channel. Reading on one device leaves stale unread badges 
on the user's other devices. Nobody can mention someone, so room conversations (which never notify) cannot reach a 
specific person. Nobody can tell in production whether messaging is healthy.
  14: 
  15: ## 3. Goals and success metrics
  16: 
  17: ### Goals
  18: - G1: A text message the user sends is never silently lost: it is delivered, pending, or visibly failed with an 
action.
  19: - G2: No message is ever stored or shown twice because of automatic resends, several tabs, lost or late 
responses, or account changes; a message is never stored under a different sender.
  20: - G3: Messaging recovers from network and Realtime outages without user action and keeps updating through 
polling while Realtime is down.
  21: - G4: Typing indicators are reliable, named, and visible only to conversation members.
  22: - G5: Unread/read state and own sent messages stay in sync across the same user's tabs and devices (≤ 5 s while 
connectivity is healthy).
  23: - G6: A user can @mention conversation members, and the mentioned person is notified on the desktop, including 
in rooms.
  24: - G7: Messaging health (latency, delivery, connection) is observable in technical logs without exposing content.
  25: - G8: No existing messaging behavior regresses; every database change reaches the online target in a controlled, 
verified way at phase end.
  26: 
  27: ### Success metrics
  28: - With ≤ 10 pending messages and create quota available, all pending messages are delivered within 10 s after 
connectivity returns, without any click, in their original order, each exactly once; with more, delivery continues 
automatically within the server rate limit (D1).
  29: - With Realtime down and HTTP working, other members' new messages appear within 45 s of the outage start, and 
within 15 s (plus request time) of being sent once polling is active.
  30: - With healthy connectivity and Realtime, cross-device/tab sync of unread counts, read state, and own sent 
messages within 5 s (D4); during a Realtime outage the polling deadlines above apply.
  31: - Each flow is covered by a passing Playwright E2E test (two accounts, and two tabs / two devices where 
relevant) that passed 3 consecutive runs in Chrome and Edge.
  32: - The existing messaging regression E2E suite passes after each slice.
  33: - Every migration of the phase is applied to the online target `vhabpcoyypobgasacsko` at phase end with explicit 
owner authorization, catalog readback, and a runtime smoke check.
  34: - Owner final test (new app against the online database) accepts the phase.
  35: 
  36: ## 4. Users and stakeholders
  37: 
  38: ### Primary users
  39: - All workspace members who use the chat in direct, group, and room conversations (members of 
`conversation_members`), as sender, recipient, or mentioned user.
  40: 
  41: ### Secondary users
  42: - The same user on several tabs of one browser and on several devices/browsers at once; several users sharing 
one browser.
  43: - The owner/operator, who reads the messaging metric logs.
  44: 
  45: ### Stakeholders
  80: - J4 Rejection: A's pending message targets a room A has since lost access to; it becomes a visible failure with 
the text kept and "Tentar de novo" / "Apagar"; later pending messages for that room wait; other conversations still 
deliver.
  81: - J5 Sign-out: A clicks Sair with 2 unsent messages; a dialog warns that leaving deletes them; Cancelar leaves A 
exactly where A was; Sair mesmo signs A out.
  82: - J6 Shared browser: A's session ends without Sair; C signs in on the same browser; C never sees A's messages 
and nothing is sent as C; when A signs in again, A's messages are sent as A.
  83: - J7 Realtime outage: after 5 s the banner shows "Reconectando…"; after 30 s the open conversation and the list 
update every 15 s; when Realtime returns, polling stops and the banner disappears.
  84: - J8 Typing: B types continuously in a group; A sees "Bruno está digitando…" the whole time; it disappears ≤ 5 s 
after B stops or leaves.
  85: - J9 Two devices: A reads part of conversation X on the laptop; within 5 s the desktop's badge and read state 
for X match.
  86: - J10 Mention: A types "@" in a room chat and picks Bruno; Bruno's tab is hidden; Bruno gets "Ana mencionou você 
em <sala>" with the full text; clicking opens the room; the message is highlighted for Bruno.
  87: - J11 Reload restore: A reloads with the drawer open on conversation X; the drawer reopens on X.
