  93: | FR-001 | Every eligible send (text and/or reply, no attachments/voice; online or offline) is first written 
durably to the current user's outbox with its `clientMessageId`, conversation, content, reply target, and requested 
mention IDs, and only then dispatched and the composer cleared. If the durable write fails, nothing is dispatched 
(FR-033). The item shows in the feed as pending while not confirmed by the server. | Must | AC-001, AC-003, AC-040 |
  94: | FR-002 | Pending items are sent automatically when connectivity returns (browser online, Realtime recovery, or 
periodic retry), per conversation in creation order, always with their own `clientMessageId`. With ≤ 10 pending and 
quota available, all are delivered within 10 s of connectivity returning; with more, delivery continues within the 
rate limit. A confirmed item becomes the normal sent message and leaves the outbox. | Must | AC-002, AC-009, AC-038 |
  95: | FR-003 | The outbox survives reload and tab close. Reloading while offline shows the browser's normal offline 
error; when the app loads again, the pending items are shown and sent. Items of the current user appear in every tab 
of the same browser. | Must | AC-004 |
  96: | FR-004 | Cross-tab ordering and ownership: the outbox order is shared by all tabs; per conversation, only the 
oldest unresolved item is eligible, and at most one tab holds the conversation's drain claim at a time (atomic claim). 
A claim is a lease: it ends when its tab closes or crashes, or when its holder exceeds the attempt deadline (request 
timeout 30 s; lease 45 s), and another tab then resumes after fencing (FR-006). When connectivity returns, an attempt 
that started before or during the outage is superseded immediately (fenced and redispatched under a new generation by 
whichever tab drains), so a hung holder never delays the D1 deadline. Across all tabs, no two create requests of the 
same conversation's outbox are in progress at once. | Must | AC-005, AC-041 |
