   9: ## Standing rules for every task
  10: 
  11: - **Migration rule (BR-014, AC-034):** during the phase a migration is done when it is written, applied to the 
LOCAL database, its tests pass, and its rollback SQL is recorded in the migration header and TRACK. Each one gets a 
row in `spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/MIGRATIONS-PENDENTES.md`. Nothing is applied online before T23.
  12: - **Old-build compatibility at introduction (§10):** every task that changes a DB contract or a route proves, 
with integration tests against the migrated local DB, that the hosted pre-Phase-4 client contract (unkeyed creates) 
and the Phase 4 client contract (keyed text/attachment/voice creates and their replays, without the new fields) keep 
working; T21 repeats this as a combined smoke with the real old builds.
  13: - **Online application method (T23 only):** the Phase 4 method (Phase 4 TRACK T2/T25): re-check `npx supabase 
migration list --linked` and the target catalog immediately before; apply only each reviewed file's SQL 
transactionally and record only its version; read back by statement hash plus catalog objects; smoke-check. Never 
`supabase db push`, `migration up --linked`, or broad `migration repair`.
  14: - **Supabase/RLS review gate (AC-035):** every migration, RLS/Realtime policy, repository, and API route change 
passes the `supabase-rls-reviewer` audit (users.id vs supabase_uid, server client + `auth.getUser()`, service role 
never replacing membership checks) before the task is done.
  15: - **Adversarial review gate (AGENTS.md):** each task's diff gets the cross-model adversarial review (direct 
Codex CLI, `gpt-6.1-sol`, effort `max`, read-only, per `delegation-anthropic.md`) before it is recorded done; findings 
fixed or rejected with reasons in TRACK. The whole work-item diff gets the same review in T22.
  16: - **Test policy (BR-015, AC-036):** integration tests against local Supabase/Realtime/real routes and Playwright 
E2E only. T1–T6 run their regression E2E through the existing local runner (`npm run test:messaging:local:e2e`); from 
T24 on, every E2E gate runs through the T24 runner (local Supabase; real Chrome and Edge projects); no unit tests; a 
touched unit test is replaced and deleted, recorded in TRACK. A new E2E spec counts only after 3 consecutive passing 
runs in Chrome and in Edge with zero retries, zero flaky, and no skipped critical test. Network shaping only (SPEC 
§15); no mocked Supabase, repositories, or code under test.
  17: - **Regression (FR-032, AC-033):** every task that changes server or drawer behavior ends with the messaging DB 
integration suite and the messaging regression E2E suite passing locally, plus type-check and lint.
  18: - **Presence touch points:** any change near sign-out or Realtime lifecycle follows the `presence-safety` skill; 
the Presence logout sequence is unchanged.
  19: - **Planning decisions under D4 (owner-adjustable):** budget infrastructure fails closed — if a create, fence, 
or metrics budget cannot be checked, the request is refused as a transient 429 (the outbox retries it) instead of 
being allowed; Phase 4 keyed requests that carry no attempt generation keep the Phase 4 keyed contract (create, replay 
200, 409) and take part in the same commit-time exclusion as fencing: such a request commits only if no fence state 
exists for its key at commit time, where fence state is created only by a fence call or a generation-carrying request 
(a generation-less create creates none, so Phase 4 retries are unaffected); a generation-less request that loses to a 
fence stores nothing and is rejected as stale. Per-stream Realtime faults in E2E may inject Phoenix channel frames 
(`phx_error`, `phx_close`) or withhold a single topic's replies on the real socket; this counts as network shaping of 
a single stream (SPEC §15) — the real transport, joins, and application callbacks stay in place and no application 
health is set directly; a real server mechanism is preferred where one exists.
  20: 
  21: ## Observations grounding this plan (2026-10-06, corrected after review r1)
  22: 
  23: - Local Supabase answers at `127.0.0.1:54321` (HTTP 200). Messaging DB suite `__tests__/messaging-db/*` 
(`vitest.messaging-db.config.mts`) and local E2E (`playwright.messaging-local.config.ts`) exist from Phase 4.
  24: - Create route (`src/app/api/messages/create/route.ts`): `clientMessageId` optional; repository 
`createWithClientKey` dedupes on unique index `(sender_id, conversation_id, client_message_id)` (migration 
`20261005000414`); the attachment path creates through a separate transactional RPC (route.ts:310). The Phase 4 
composer sends a key for text, attachment, and voice creates (`message-composer.tsx:223`, `useMessages.ts:284`). No 
attempt generation, fence/lookup route, or expected-sender field. Early validation (route.ts:231) runs before any 
budget is charged.
  25: - Rate limiting: `enforceRateLimit` (`src/lib/auth/rate-limit.ts`) fails open on RPC error (line 48); 
`check_rate_limit` (`20260612190000`) increments a fixed-window counter on every call, including denied ones — an 
attempt counter, not a winning-insert quota.
